            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0530" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/68</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-10T01:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 10, 1914, 1 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 11, 4:45 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Foreign Office communicates list of articles and materials which the German
                    Government, pursuant to Nos. 21 and 23 of the prize ordinance of September 30,
                    1909, <hi rendition="#italic">Reichs-Gesetzblatt</hi>, page 275, declares
                    contraband of war. They correspond exactly, as regards absolute contraband, to
                    Article 22, Nos. 1 to 11 inclusive, of the Declaration of London; and, as
                    regards conditional contraband, to Article 24, Nos. 1 to 14. They further state
                    that the ordinance mentioned contains the substance of the Declaration of
                    London; that Germany will apply these laws provided that the other belligerents
                    do not disregard them.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office requests to be informed regarding attitude of the other
                    powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
